### MAJ-CORR-002: test_scaffold_downstream.sh edge case when main HEAD == v1.2.0 SHA

**Bug:** in tests/scaffolder/test_scaffold_downstream.sh, SCP_SHA_POST_V1_2_0 derived from `git rev-parse main`. Edge case: if main HEAD equals the v1.2.0 tag SHA exactly (rare but possible if main hasn't moved since v1.2.0 cut), the post-v1.2.0 warn assertion fails because the SHA isn't actually post-v1.2.0.

**Fix:** in tests/scaffolder/test_scaffold_downstream.sh, add a guard before the post-v1.2.0 assertion block:
```bash
v1_2_0_sha="$(git -C "$REPO_ROOT" rev-parse v1.2.0 2>/dev/null || echo 'TAG_ABSENT')"
if [ "$SCP_SHA_POST_V1_2_0" != "$v1_2_0_sha" ] && [ "$v1_2_0_sha" != "TAG_ABSENT" ]; then
  # existing post-v1.2.0 assertion
  grep -Fq 'post-v1.2.0' "$stderr_file" || fail 'post-v1.2.0 warning missing'
else
  echo 'SKIP: SCP_SHA_POST_V1_2_0 equals v1.2.0 tag SHA OR tag absent; cannot test post-v1.2.0 warn path' >&2
fi
```

This is consistent with the existing v1.2.0-tag-absent SKIP pattern.

